{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1163149-new-york-city","id":1163149,"title":"New York City","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-27T20:05:22-08:00","id":1163149,"title":"New York City","content":"Who controls New York City? David, Queen Mab or a Duke? Very confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4045-princeofcincinnati","name":"princeofcincinnati","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4045_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T17:09:13-08:00","id":1163765,"title":"","content":"I would presume it's analogous to Donald Trump, Andrew Cuomo, Bill de Blasio, and the various Borough Presidents. While Gov. Cuomo, for example, has a great deal of authority throughout the state, he doesn't manage the day to day affairs of NYC. <br /> <br /> David is High King of Concordia, Mab is Queen of the Kingdom of Apples, whomever the Duke of (New York State), the Count of (New York City), and the Barons of the various Boroughs, each of whom has varying levels of authority, with the greater the authority, the more areas they have competing for their attention. The Baroness of (whatever Staten Island is called) can be hyper focused on whats going on in her immediate territory, while Queen Mab has several states worth of problems and politics to juggle. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T20:33:24-08:00","id":1163806,"title":"","content":"Duke Kelodin, a Troll Grump of House Fiona who was ennobled after the accordance war, is the Duke of New York State. His primary freehold is in Buffalo, but he owns another in Manhattan. Unless you create an NPC beneath him (a Count, Baron, Knight, Squire, Mayor or simple Freeholder) to represent New York City itself, then Duke Kelodin is the immediate ruler of NYC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19264-slanzer","name":"Slanzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}